{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7Js7cpWCYVGaRB1ZLwF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before I draft this, five questions. Your answers will change what the email says:\n\n1. **Which September, and which year-end?** Today is 16 November 2026. If the change starts 1 September 2027, then \"end of next year\" gives the four long-distance people only four months beyond everyone else. Is that what you mean, or do they keep remote work until the end of 2028?\n\n2. **What about the other 11 people hired as fully remote?** They live within two hours, but they took the job on remote terms and may have arranged their lives around that. Are you offering them anything, such as help with travel costs, a later start date or a conversation one-to-one? If someone can't make it work, what happens? Can they ask for an exception or leave on agreed terms? If the email says nothing, people will assume the worst.\n\n3. **Is there an exceptions process?** I mean for things like caring responsibilities, health or disability. If so, who do people talk to?\n\n4. **What's decided and what's still open on Friday?** I assume the three days are fixed. Is anything up for discussion, like which three days or how Mondays and Fridays work?\n\n5. **Who is it from?** Should it come from all three partners together or from you? Please give the names as they should appear in the sign-off.\n\nIf you don't know some of these yet, say so. I'll write around those gaps rather than guess."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":254,"cache_read_input_tokens":9539,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":254},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":